From 66ee28c576f55902545aa77380f595acf064b1da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:16:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tools: handover sim can render the E2 run to a video and
 shoot still views of the standing G1 (0116; probe e2 calls render_results
 before every env.step and end_render_results at the end, the same path as the
 door evaluation VIDEO=1 of 0015 and 0089, so each frame matches one 50 Hz
 record row; render_eye_rel and render_target_rel place the fixed camera in
 the frame of env cam_env robot at reset, cam_yaw_deg overrides its heading
 since the robot yaw is random per env and turns while hanging, hide_scene
 makes the door, the goal markers and the other robots invisible without
 touching physics, no_reset keeps the termination flags but does not reset the
 env so the fall stays on the video, with fell_t counted as before; the new
 probe views hands the robot over, releases the rope and saves PNGs from given
 views with the camera pose, intrinsics and joint angles in views_camera.json,
 optionally again with the floor hidden; simfix_probe enables cameras only
 with render_results; simulator.config.render_focal_length sets the evaluation
 camera focal length; on 11-18 the 18 env E2 with rendering reproduced the
 10-26 E2 rows, joint angles of env 16 identical up to its fall and of env 4
 over the whole run; default off = unchanged) (11-18)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
